      "type": "atom",
      "label": "Skills evolved against a 4B model improved a 9B model without retraining, which is evidence that the maintained text carries the capability rather than the weights."
    },
    {
      "id": "atom:atom-2",
      "type": "atom",
      "label": "Prefer primary sources: a blog post summarizing a paper is not the paper. Cite the paper or say you could not reach it."
    },
    {
      "id": "atom:atom-3",
      "type": "atom",
      "label": "Only include work from the last 24 months unless it is foundational to the question, and say which it is."
    },
    {
      "id": "atom:atom-4",
      "type": "atom",
      "label": "Open question: does the cross-model transfer result hold when the harness changes too, not just the model? Untested as far as we can tell."
    },
    {
      "id": "atom:atom-5",
      "type": "atom",
      "label": "Giving the executing agent write access to its own wiki during evolution degraded final skill quality, so execution and maintenance were kept as separate roles."
    }
